course: dictionary
lesson: 13131
title: A formal word for food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are formal. You meet them more in science lessons, on food labels and in the news than in everyday chat. «Foodstuff» is one of these. It is a noun, so it names a thing, and it means any substance used as food. When there is more than one, you write foodstuffs.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «The shop sells basic foodstuffs like bread, rice and milk.» The words bread, rice and milk are clues: they are all things we eat, so foodstuffs must mean food of this kind. Ask yourself what word would fit, then swap in "food" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Formal words often appear in lists or serious writing. «Countries trade foodstuffs with each other.» In a geography lesson, this means countries buy and sell food to one another. The everyday word is food, so when you meet foodstuff, think "food" and check that the sentence still works.
fact: Foodstuff means any substance used as food.
fact: Foodstuffs is the plural, used for more than one kind of food.
fact: «The label lists all the foodstuffs in the tin.» Here it means all the food inside the tin.
fact: Examples of foodstuffs are bread, rice, meat and milk.
fact: Foodstuff is a formal word; the everyday word for it is food.
exercise: «The shop sells basic foodstuffs like bread, rice and milk.» What does foodstuffs mean here? | Empty boxes | Shop lights | Clothes and shoes | *Food of many kinds
exercise: Mia says foodstuff is a fancy word for food. Is she right? | *Yes, foodstuff means any substance used as food | No, foodstuff means a sort of cloth | No, foodstuff means a kitchen | Not sure, it means a type of car
exercise: Which everyday word could replace foodstuffs in «The label lists all the foodstuffs in the tin.»? | Label | Tin | Lists | *Food
test: What is the plural of foodstuff? | foodstuffes | *foodstuffs | foodstuffies | foodstuff's
test: Which of these is an example of a foodstuff? | A bag | *Rice | A plate | A spoon
exam: Which sentence uses foodstuffs correctly? | «The foodstuff ran fast along the track.» | *«The farm sends foodstuffs to the city.» | «He foodstuffed the door shut.» | «My foodstuffs are blue and loud.»
